'\" t
.\" kushare manual page (English; installed as the default page). The Spanish
.\" one is ../es/kushare.1: keep both in sync. When adding a CLI command, add it
.\" to both: the test `man_page_lists_every_command` (src/main.rs) checks it.
.TH KUSHARE 1 "2026-11-25" "kushare" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
kushare \- files, notifications and your phone between a Linux PC and Android
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B kushare
.RB [ \-\-device\-name
.IR NAME ]
.RB [ \-\-port
.IR PORT ]
.RB [ \-\-link\-port
.IR PORT ]
.br
.B kushare
.I COMMAND
.RI [ ARGUMENTS ...]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B kushare
is a Quick Share (formerly Nearby Share) client for Linux with a
.B persistent link
to the
.B kushare\-android
app, in the style of KDE Connect or Phone Link:
notifications synced both ways, battery, media, calls, SMS, photos, clipboard,
and the phone as a webcam, microphone or QR scanner for the PC.
.PP
Without a
.I COMMAND
it starts the
.BR daemon :
tray icon, file reception over TCP and Bluetooth RFCOMM, mDNS announcement,
the link with paired devices and the
.B org.kushare.Daemon
D-Bus API on the session bus. It is normally started by the desktop session
.RI ( /etc/xdg/autostart/kushare.desktop )
or by the systemd user service
.RB ( "systemctl \-\-user enable \-\-now kushare" ).
Only one daemon can run per session.
.PP
The other commands are D-Bus clients of the daemon (except
.BR send ,
which works on its own, and
.BR send\-bt ,
which uses the daemon if it is running). Wherever a
.I DEVICE
is expected, its id, an id prefix or its name are accepted, as shown by
.BR "kushare devices" .
.PP
Control traffic always goes over Bluetooth; Wi-Fi is opened only for heavy
transfers (photos, SMS, webcam) and closes by itself.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BI \-\-device\-name " NAME"
Name of this computer as others will see it. Defaults to one derived from the
hostname. Also accepted after any command.
.TP
.BI \-\-port " PORT"
TCP port for receiving files over Quick Share. 0 (the default) lets the system
pick a free one. Daemon only.
.TP
.BI \-\-link\-port " PORT"
TCP port of the persistent link (default 47816, fixed so it can be opened in
the firewall). If it is taken, another free one is used.
.TP
.BR \-h ", " \-\-help
Show help (also
.BI "kushare help" " COMMAND"
or
.IB COMMAND " \-\-help"
for each command).
.TP
.BR \-V ", " \-\-version
Show the version.
.SH COMMANDS
.SS Files
.TP
.BI "send " "FILE ADDRESS"
Send a file straight to
.IR host:port ,
without the daemon or discovery. Useful for testing.
.TP
.BI "send\-bt " "FILE MAC"
Send a file over Bluetooth RFCOMM to an already bonded device
.RB ( "bluetoothctl pair" ),
with no IP network. If the daemon is running it does the transfer (BlueZ only
allows one registration of the profile per computer).
.SS Devices and pairing
.TP
.B devices
List paired devices (with their connection state) and those found in the last
scan.
.TP
.BR scan " [" \fISECONDS\fR ]
Look for kushare devices on the network (15 s by default). There is no
continuous scanning, to save battery.
.TP
.BR pair " [" \-\-yes "] " \fIDEVICE\fR
Pair with a device visible on the network (id, prefix or name) or over
Bluetooth (MAC of an already bonded device). Both sides show the same PIN;
.B \-\-yes
accepts it here without asking.
.TP
.BI "unpair " DEVICE
Forget a paired device, on both sides.
.TP
.B quit
Stop the running daemon.
.TP
.B doctor
Diagnose common problems (port, firewall, mDNS, Bluetooth, notifications,
audio) and explain how to fix them.
.SS Notifications
.TP
.BI "notif on" \fR|\fPoff " DEVICE" \fR\ [\fPin\fR|\fPout\fR|\fPboth\fR]\fP
Turn notifications with a device on or off:
.B in
receives its notifications here,
.B out
sends this computer's to it,
.B both
(the default) does both.
.TP
.BI "apps " DEVICE
Known apps and which ones are blocked.
.TP
.BI "block " "DEVICE DIRECTION APP"
.PD 0
.TP
.BI "unblock " "DEVICE DIRECTION APP"
.PD
Block or unblock an app's notifications in one direction
.RB ( in ", " out " or " both ).
.TP
.BR phone\-notifs " [" \-\-dismiss " \fIKEY\fR] \fIDEVICE\fR"
Notifications currently on the phone;
.B \-\-dismiss
dismisses one.
.SS Phone
.TP
.BI "status " DEVICE
Battery, ringer, call, media players and audio outputs.
.TP
.BI "media " "DEVICE ACTION" \fR\ [\fPPLAYER\fR]\fP
Control its media players.
.I ACTION
is
.BR play\-pause ", " play ", " pause ", " next ", " previous " or " stop .
Without a player it acts on all of them
.RB ( "kushare media phone pause"
= pause everything).
.TP
.BI "audio " DEVICE \fR\ [\fPOUTPUT\fR]\fP
List its audio outputs or choose one (id or part of the name). Android does not
let an app switch the output of other apps: from the PC it is read-only.
.TP
.BR find " [" \-\-stop "] \fIDEVICE\fR"
Ring the phone to find it, even when it is on silent.
.TP
.BI "ringer " DEVICE " normal" \fR|\fPvibrate\fR|\fPsilent
Change the ringer mode.
.TP
.BI "call " "DEVICE ACTION"
Control the ongoing call:
.BR answer ", " reject ", " hangup ", " mute " or " unmute .
.TP
.BI "dtmf " "DEVICE DIGITS"
DTMF tones in the ongoing call (voice menus, extensions):
.RB \(lq 1 \(rq,
.RB \(lq 123# \(rq.
.TP
.BI "dial " "DEVICE NUMBER"
Call from the phone. Letters are accepted
.RB ( 1\-800\-FLOWERS ).
.TP
.BI "phone\-audio " DEVICE " on" \fR|\fPoff
Hear the phone's music and calls on the PC (Bluetooth A2DP and HFP).
.TP
.BI "calls " DEVICE
Call log
.RB ( \-\-limit ,
20 by default).
.TP
.BI "contacts " DEVICE \fR\ [\fPSEARCH\fR]\fP
Search the contacts.
.TP
.BI "sms " DEVICE
SMS conversations.
.BI \-\-thread " ID"
shows its messages;
.BI \-\-to " NUMBER TEXT"
sends an SMS;
.B \-\-limit
how many (20).
.TP
.BI "photos " DEVICE
Photos on the phone, newest first
.RB ( \-\-offset ", " \-\-limit ).
.BI \-\-download " ID"
downloads the original to the downloads folder;
.BI \-\-delete " ID"
moves it to the phone's trash (it may ask for confirmation there).
.SS The phone as a PC peripheral
.TP
.BR "mic start" \fR|\fPstop\fR|\fPstatus
The phone as a microphone: an input named after the phone appears
.RB ( kushare_mic ).
Requires
.BR pactl .
.TP
.BR "webcam cameras" \fR|\fPstart\fR|\fPstop\fR|\fPstatus
The phone as a webcam (v4l2loopback or PipeWire).
.B start \-\-camera
accepts the id or part of the label, as listed by
.BR cameras .
.TP
.BR "qr scan" \fR|\fPlist\fR|\fPopen\fR|\fPcopy\fR|\fPsave\fR|\fPforget
The phone's QR scanner and the history of scanned codes. The number shown by
.B list
is the one the others take;
.B open
only opens http/https web pages;
.B forget \-\-all
clears everything.
.SS Share internet
.TP
.BR "hotspot on" " [" \-\-switch\-antenna "] | " off " | " status " | " qr
The PC creates its own Wi-Fi network and shares its internet with the phone.
.B on
turns it on (it may ask for the administrator password through polkit) and
shows the QR code to connect with the camera;
.B qr
shows it again. The Wi-Fi card stays connected to its network: the access
point uses the same channel ("no IR" channels, such as 36–48 on many cards,
cannot be used; see
.BR "kushare doctor" ).
If the PC's network has another antenna on a valid channel, it offers to
switch to it (or does so without asking with
.BR \-\-switch\-antenna )
while the network is on; turning it off restores everything.
.TP
.BR "hotspot config" " [" \-\-ssid " \fINAME\fR] [" \-\-password " \fIPASSWORD\fR | " \-\-random ]
Network name and WPA2 password (8–63 ASCII characters); applied when it is
turned on.
.TP
.BI "hotspot send " DEVICE
Send the network to the phone over the link: it asks whether to connect, with
no scanning.
.SS This PC
.TP
.BR clipboard " [" \-\-clear "] [" \-\-copy " \fIN\fR]"
Shared clipboard history.
.TP
.BR setting " [\fINAME\fR " on \fR|\fP off ]
Daemon settings; without arguments it lists them:
.TS
tab(@);
lB l.
clipboard\-sync@share the clipboard with the phone
clipboard\-history@keep a clipboard history
photo\-prefetch@preload thumbnails (Wi-Fi only)
update\-check@check for new versions at startup
receive\-confirm@ask before accepting a file
photo\-notify@notify about new photos with a thumbnail
hybrid@Wi-Fi on demand for heavy transfers
dynamic\-lock@lock the session when the phone goes away
.TE
.TP
.BR pc\-audio " [" \-\-output " \fIOUTPUT\fR] [" \-\-input " \fIINPUT\fR]"
Audio outputs and inputs of this PC; with an option, choose the default one
(id or part of the name).
.TP
.BR update " [" \-\-download ]
Check GitHub for a new version;
.B \-\-download
downloads it and verifies it against
.BR SHA256SUMS .
.SH FILES
.TP
.I ~/.config/kushare/
.B identity.key
(this computer's Ed25519 identity; do not share),
.B peers.toml
(paired devices and filters),
.B daemon.toml
(settings),
.B gui.toml
(interface),
.B language
(chosen language).
.TP
.I ~/.local/share/kushare/
Clipboard and QR history.
.TP
.I ~/.config/kushare/hotspot.toml
Name and password of the "Share internet" network (readable only by the
user).
.TP
.IR /usr/lib/kushare/kushare\-hotspot ", " /usr/share/polkit\-1/actions/org.kushare.hotspot.policy
Root helper for the access point (iw + hostapd) and its polkit rule.
.TP
.I ~/.cache/kushare/
Thumbnails, photos, cover art, icons, contact photos and phone wallpapers.
Safe to delete; it has a size limit.
.TP
.I /usr/lib/systemd/user/kushare.service
User service (not enabled automatically).
.TP
.IR ~/.local/share/kushare/locales/ ", " /usr/share/kushare/locales/
Extra translations
.RI ( language .json,
a translated copy of
.BR es.json );
Spanish and English are built into the binary.
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
.B KUSHARE_LANG
Interface language
.RB ( es ", " en );
takes precedence over the one chosen in the GUI and over
.BR LC_ALL ", " LC_MESSAGES " and " LANG .
.TP
.B KUSHARE_LOCALE_DIR
Alternative translations directory.
.TP
.B RUST_LOG
Daemon log level (e.g.
.BR info,kushare=debug ).
.SH EXAMPLES
Pair the phone over Bluetooth and show its status:
.PP
.RS
.nf
bluetoothctl pair AA:BB:CC:DD:EE:FF
kushare pair AA:BB:CC:DD:EE:FF
kushare status phone
.fi
.RE
.PP
Pause everything playing on the phone and silence it:
.PP
.RS
.nf
kushare media phone pause
kushare ringer phone silent
.fi
.RE
.PP
Use the front camera as a webcam and download the latest photo:
.PP
.RS
.nf
kushare webcam start \-\-camera front
kushare photos phone \-\-limit 1
kushare photos phone \-\-download ID
.fi
.RE
.SH SECURITY
Only paired devices (PIN on both sides and Ed25519 keys) can use the link;
everything is encrypted. Files received over Quick Share are only accepted
after asking. More details in
.IR /usr/share/doc/kushare/SECURITY.md .
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR kushare\-gui (1),
.BR kushare\-tui (1),
.BR bluetoothctl (1),
.BR pactl (1).
.PP
.I /usr/share/doc/kushare/README.md
and
.I FAQ.md
(common problems);
https://github.com/tysyak/kushare
